L0121: Invalid attribute arguments

A recognized attribute has the wrong argument shape. For example, no_panic takes no arguments, derive takes a parenthesized trait list, and a termination measure uses its documented decreases form. Match the attribute grammar before checking its semantic promise.

Example from `tests/corpus/reject/attribute_shape.lc`; the full file is a regression test.

```locus
// An attribute of the closed set in a shape it does not have.
#[no_panic(always)]
fn first(n: u8) -> u8 { n }

#[derive]
struct Lock { failures: u8 }

#[terminates(fuel = 3)]
fn second(n: u8) -> u8 { n }
```

Language, as built: [1.25:2](../../atlas.html#/doc/language/spec-1.25:2).
